Final message:
The commit introduces a real regression: `subtotal()`'s loop bound was changed to `items.length - 1`, which drops the last line item from every total — this contradicts the existing test and will also corrupt `discounted()`/`total()`. Additionally, `discounted()` doesn't guard against a negative or >100 percent (would add a surcharge instead of discounting), and no new tests were added for the discount feature itself. I'd fix the loop bound before anything else — that one's silently wrong for every invoice with more than one line.
